    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_6e51b420",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a group of men in a social setting, with one prominently holding a cup and wearing a Miami Heat jersey. The overlaid text reads: 'when you successfully shot all the muslims in the mosque but isis doesn't claim the assault.' This text is a hateful and violent metaphor that equates the act of mass murder of Muslims in a mosque with a supposed 'success' that is not claimed by ISIS. The meme uses the juxtaposition of a casual, celebratory image (men drinking, partying) with a horrific, genocidal act to create a jarring and offensive contrast. The intent is to normalize or trivialize the killing of Muslims in a mosque by implying it is somehow 'successful' or 'unclaimed' by ISIS, which is a direct attack on the Muslim community and promotes Islamophobia. The meme is designed to incite hatred and fear toward Muslims by associating them with terrorism and suggesting that their suffering is somehow not 'officially' recognized or claimed by the terrorist group responsible, which is a dangerous and hateful distortion of reality.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_eacb77d8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
